  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="83f4c3f1-3e49-5b11-a084-ba9ed6044846" activityNameId="7615e87c-a27d-5f53-a279-ded739f49479" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, high speed train</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, high speed train
For rail infrastructure, expenditures and environmental interventions due to construction, renewal and disposal of railway tracks have been allocated based on the train kilometric performance of an average German ICE train 417182 vkm and a life time of  40 years .  For the determination of the train demand the yearly transport performance of ICE trains in Germany was used 97837945 pkm.;
UUID: b78d3312-efbb-34fa-8f13-0fb54e6650ca
The module calls the modules  "production, maintenance and disposal of vehicles"; "construction and maintenance and disposal of railway tracks". The module includes the energy consumption and emission of the train operation.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: For vehicle operation all technologies  are included in the average data. Rail construction addresses conventional and modern ballastless beddings.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: 97837945 pkm
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: Emission, extrapolated from long distance train transport in CH
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b78d3312-efbb-34fa-8f13-0fb54e6650ca.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="902c7f79-ee40-5428-a5fc-c3857aed91e4" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
